# Suderra OS — U-Boot environment (fw_setenv/fw_printenv) configuration (ARM,
# ADR-048 DEC-18).
#
# RAUC's U-Boot backend writes BOOT_ORDER and BOOT_<slot>_LEFT here; U-Boot's
# compiled-in bootcmd (board/suderra/uboot/suderra.env) reads the same variables
# and chooses the slot. The environment is two raw, CRC-checked copies on the
# boot disk, in the gap in front of the first partition (genimage-prod.cfg starts
# the boot partition at 1 MiB), not a file on the boot FAT: /boot is read-only
# except while RAUC installs, and a power cut while one copy is written leaves the
# other valid. Two lines make fw_setenv write both the way U-Boot's
# SYS_REDUNDAND_ENVIRONMENT does (flag byte, newer copy wins).
#
# The offsets and the size are U-Boot's CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET, CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET_REDUND
# and CONFIG_ENV_SIZE (board/suderra/aarch64-rpi4/uboot-fragment.config);
# tests/image-contracts/uboot-env-contract-test.sh holds the three files equal.
# /dev/mmcblk0 is the eMMC or SD card U-Boot reads as mmc 0 (the SD/eMMC
# controller is mmc0 in the device tree of every board of this family).
#
# <device>      <offset>    <env size>
/dev/mmcblk0    0x60000     0x4000
/dev/mmcblk0    0x80000     0x4000
